  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "S01",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 12,
      "frames": 360,
      "words": 19,
      "planned_slot_wpm": 95.0,
      "text": "One captured payment. Two active orders. For a merchant, which order should ship? This is OrderTruth's controlled reference store.",
      "pieces": [
        {
          "source": "deterministic",
          "in": 51.985,
          "out": 63.988
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S02",
      "start": 12,
      "end": 25,
      "frames": 390,
      "words": 27,
      "planned_slot_wpm": 124.6,
      "text": "A public checkout bug report describes this kind of mismatch. A payment can succeed while the merchant's order state is wrong, risking duplicate fulfillment and manual investigation.",
      "pieces": [
        {
          "source": "S02",
          "in": 0,
          "out": 6.0
        },
        {
          "source": "deterministic",
          "in": 51.985,
          "out": 58.985
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S03",
      "start": 25,
      "end": 32,
      "frames": 210,
      "words": 9,
      "planned_slot_wpm": 77.1,
      "text": "OrderTruth connects the payment evidence to the merchant outcome.",
      "pieces": [
        {
          "source": "S03",
          "in": 0,
          "out": 7.0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S04",
      "start": 32,
      "end": 50,
      "frames": 540,
      "words": 30,
      "planned_slot_wpm": 100.0,
      "text": "This case references a genuine, previously captured PayPal Sandbox payment, verified through an Orders API readback. We reuse that stored observation. No new payment is taken to create this case.",
      "pieces": [
        {
          "source": "deterministic",
          "in": 18.155,
          "out": 36.171
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S05",
      "start": 50,
      "end": 65,
      "frames": 450,
      "words": 29,
      "planned_slot_wpm": 116.0,
      "text": "For this reference merchant, one purchase should leave one active order. I introduce a labelled merchant-side duplicate. Deterministic checks detect two active orders linked to the same payment observation.",
      "pieces": [
        {
          "source": "deterministic",
          "in": 36.727,
          "out": 39.74
        },
        {
          "source": "deterministic",
          "in": 39.74,
          "out": 41.24
        },
        {
          "source": "deterministic",
          "in": 41.498,
          "out": 44.501
        },
        {
          "source": "deterministic",
          "in": 44.501,
          "out": 46.001
        },
        {
          "source": "deterministic",
          "in": 47.968,
          "out": 51.985
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S06",
      "start": 65,
      "end": 78,
      "frames": 390,
      "words": 24,
      "planned_slot_wpm": 110.8,
      "text": "Autopilot is available in the application. This recording uses deterministic findings because its live free allowance is unverified. No model response is being presented for this case.",
      "pieces": [
        {
          "source": "deterministic",
          "in": 64.534,
          "out": 77.546
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S07",
      "start": 78,
      "end": 102,
      "frames": 720,
      "words": 41,
      "planned_slot_wpm": 102.5,
      "text": "The finding is specific: two active merchant orders reference the same recorded payment observation. That establishes a discrepancy, not its cause. The controlled fault demonstrates the reference merchant's contract; it is not a reproduction of the external checkout bug.",
      "pieces": [
        {
          "source": "deterministic",
          "in": 77.546,
          "out": 101.547
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S08",
      "start": 102,
      "end": 114,
      "frames": 360,
      "words": 26,
      "planned_slot_wpm": 130.0,
      "text": "The next decision belongs to the merchant. A hypothesis is not permission to change an order, and no AI output can authorize the correction.",
      "pieces": [
        {
          "source": "deterministic",
          "in": 101.547,
          "out": 113.563
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S09",
      "start": 114,
      "end": 133,
      "frames": 570,
      "words": 35,
      "planned_slot_wpm": 110.5,
      "text": "Here is the exact correction proposal: keep Merchant order one and void Merchant order two locally. Approval and execution are separate. Neither has been performed in this recording.",
      "pieces": [
        {
          "source": "deterministic",
          "in": 115.497,
          "out": 121.512
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S10",
      "start": 133,
      "end": 151,
      "frames": 540,
      "words": 31,
      "planned_slot_wpm": 103.3,
      "text": "Execution and receipt verification are still awaiting authorization. This review cut does not show a completed correction. The final film must reopen the persisted receipt and verify one active matching order.",
      "pieces": [
        {
          "source": "deterministic",
          "in": 115.497,
          "out": 121.512
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S11",
      "start": 151,
      "end": 162,
      "frames": 330,
      "words": 14,
      "planned_slot_wpm": 76.4,
      "text": "OrderTruth connects payment evidence to merchant outcomes. This review cut reaches the exact correction proposal. The verified outcome remains pending.",
      "pieces": [
        {
